Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.00,0:02:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.13,0:02:29.30,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you want to talk about?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.17,0:02:31.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.59,0:02:35.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Mayuri will die in two hours?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.47,0:02:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,You've time leaped and seen it over and over.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.94,0:02:48.31,Default,,0,0,0,,That must've been painful.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.19,0:02:53.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Given what Amane said,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.99,0:02:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,we need to go from the Alpha \NAttractor Field, where we are now,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.24,0:03:00.99,Default,,0,0,0,,to the Beta worldline in order to save Mayuri.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.16,0:03:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,To do that,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.41,0:03:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,we need the IBN 5100 to delete SERN's data on you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.92,0:03:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,But the IBN 5100 that used to be at Yanabayashi Shrine
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.38,0:03:16.84,Default,,0,0,0,,disappeared when the worldline moved.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.22,0:03:21.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The worldlines moved when you sent the following D-Mails:
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.43,0:03:21.76,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\be3\an2\fs57\pos(1296,513)\c&HDCC9CF&}Hououin Kyouma
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.43,0:03:21.76,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\be3\an2\fs60\c&HDCC9CF&\pos(1296,615)}(No Subject)
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.64,0:03:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The LOTO SIX,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.76,0:03:22.43,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\be3\an2\fs57\pos(1296,513)\c&HDCC9CF&}Hououin Kyouma
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.76,0:03:22.43,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\be3\an2\fs60\c&HDCC9CF&\pos(1296,615)}(No Subject)
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.76,0:03:22.27,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\be3\an2\c&HDCC9CF&\fs67.5\pos(675,813)}Buy LOTO SIX
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.27,0:03:22.43,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\be3\an2\c&HDCC9CF&\fs67.5\pos(675,813)}You'll win!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.81,0:03:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Kiryu's,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.85,0:03:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Urushibara's,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.64,0:03:25.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Faris's,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.98,0:03:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,and the one about tailing Amane.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.19,0:03:27.65,Sign1,,0,0,0,,{\an4\be5\pos(307.5,744)\frz353.614\fax-0.05\frx0\fry0}Do not give in to your assistant's threats. \NFollow Suzuha!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.77,0:03:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,When you undid the one about following Amane,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.36,0:03:33.32,Default,,0,0,0,,the attack was delayed by one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.90,0:03:34.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That means,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.36,0:03:38.03,Default,,0,0,0,,if you go back and undo the other D-Mails,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.03,0:03:42.41,Default,,0,0,0,,you could return to the worldline that had the IBN 5100, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.33,0:03:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It's just a theory.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.58,0:03:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no definitive proof.
